.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-TEST 1
.Os Wattle 0.3.0
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-test
.Nd run the tests of a project
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle test"
.Oo
.Ar options
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle test"
runs each file ending in
.Ql "\&.wattle"
under
.Eo
.Pa ./test/
.Ec
in the current directory.
Each file runs in a separate process.
.Ic t
is a synonym for
.Cm test .
.Pp
The output begins with
.Ql "seed:"
and the seed used to determine the test order.
Each file then has a summary line with a result mark,
its path and the counts of tests and assertions.
Output from a failed file is printed below its summary,
with a border that is red when colour is enabled.
Output from a successful file is not printed.
.Pp
The final summary gives the number of files and tests and lists
the files that failed.
The exit status is 1 if any file failed or no file was run.
.Pp
Test files that use the Gum test module,
.Eo
.Pa gum/test.wattle
.Ec ,
read the dynamic bindings set by
.Fl t ,
.Fl T
and
.Fl "-seed" .
These options select tests within a file and control their order.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl f ,
.Fl "-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Run only the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path ,
which is relative to
.Eo
.Pa ./test/
.Ec .
This option can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl F .
.It Xo
.Fl F ,
.Fl "-no-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Skips the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path ,
relative to
.Eo
.Pa ./test/
.Ec .
This option can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl f .
.It Xo
.Fl t ,
.Fl "-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/tests"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl T .
.It Xo
.Fl T ,
.Fl "-no-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/skips"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl t .
.It Xo
.Fl "-seed"
.Ar seed
.Xc
Use the integer
.Ar seed
to seed the generator that shuffles the test files.
The command also sets the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/seed" ,
which Gum test files use to shuffle their tests.
Without
.Fl "-seed" ,
the seed is taken from the clock,
so the order varies between runs.
The same seed gives the same order.
.It Xo
.Fl b ,
.Fl "-bail"
.Xc
Stop after the first test file that fails.
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-lint-error"
.Ar level ,
.Fl w ,
.Fl "-lint-warn"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint levels of each test file.
They take the same values as for
.Ic wattle
.Cm check .
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run the tests in
.Eo
.Pa ./test/
.Ec ,
skipping one file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle test --no-file slow\&.wattle
.Ed
.
